Package: dux
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: dux maintainers <root@localhost>
Recommends: curl, bsdutils | util-linux
Suggests: smartmontools
Description: disk-full alerts, folder attribution and safe cleanup
 dux watches free space and inodes on every disk (every minute, every 5
 seconds once a disk is past its warning level) and alerts through the
 system log, ntfy, Slack, a webhook, email and wall: once per level, when
 clearly worse, and on recovery. It says which folder grew and who writes
 it, finds logs, Docker data, projects and caches, and offers cleanup rated
 SAFE, CAUTION or RISKY. Automatic cleanup is off unless you approve it.
 Includes a terminal UI, a read-only web dashboard with an API and
 Prometheus metrics. Set up with: dux setup
